    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="20">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Grith">Grið</ref> 20</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="20" corresp="#wit-g-b"><pb n="472" ed="#liebermann"/>Se þe oferhogie þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> he heom hlyste, hæbbe him gemæne þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> wið God sylfne<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Grith_20.lnote.oe.1"/>.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" n="20" corresp="#wit-g-b"><pb n="26" ed="#rabin-doml"/>Se þe oferhogie þæt he heom hlyste, hæbbe him gemæne þæt wið God sylfne.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="472" ed="#liebermann"/>Wer verschmäht, auf sie zu hören, habe das zu verantworten bei Gott selbst.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">Whoever scorns to listen to them, let him answer for it to God himself.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-b"><pb n="27" ed="#rabin-doml"/>Anyone who rejects what he hears from them must settle his dispute with God himself.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="472"><ref target="clause:ICn_26-4">I Cn 26.4</ref></note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">I Cn. 26, 4</note>
        <note type="editorial">Liebermann compares I Cn 26.; T: corrected against Rabin, DOML 66 (2020), p. 26 (before: ‘Se þe oferhogie þæt he heom hlyste, hæbbe him gemaene þæt wið God sylfne.’)</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Grith_20.lnote.oe.1" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">472</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">syfne, <hi rend="italic">übergeschr.</hi> l</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">syfne, l written above</seg></note>
      </div>
    </body>
